.TH LPQ 1
.UC
.SH NAME
lpq \- show lineprinter queue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlpq\fR [ option ] [ job_numbers ... ] [ user_names ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fILpq\fR displays the \fIfiles\fR that are queued for printing on a line
printer.  Any job numbers or user names entered with the command will limit
the output to jobs with the appropriate job numbers or that have been printed
by the users whose names were given.  The
following
.IR option s
are available:
.TP \w'-Pprinter\ \ \ 'u
.B \-\^l
Display the queue with a long format.
.TP
.B \-\^Pprinter
Display the queue for printer
.IR printer .
.SH FILES
.ta 2i
/usr/spool/lpd/lock
.br
/usr/spool/lpd/cf*	data file
.br
/usr/spool/lpd/df*	daemon control file
.br
/usr/spool/lpd/tf*	temporary version of control file
.DT
.SH SEE ALSO
lpq(1), lprm(1), printcap(5), lpd(8), ulf(8)
